{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/920033-gifts-of-numen-for-your-use","id":920033,"title":"Gifts of Numen - for your use","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-23T17:40:15-07:00","id":920033,"title":"Gifts of Numen - for your use","content":"Hello dear friends! In my game Seventh Seal, the ghost wolf PC has access to a unique gift list that, while others can learn, is so far specific to her. Because she's Ithaeur and wanted to go for a sort of sorceress thing, I thought these gifts worked well for her , and it's been fun watching her use them.<br /> <br /> You can obviously use and change them as you wish.<br /> <br /> Blast (Wisdom): Instant. Spend 1 Essence. Roll Int+Occult, dealing successes+Wisdom in lethal damage, with range equal to Wisdom*10. Add 2 essence to increase damage by 1.)<br /> <br /> -Armor (Honor): Reflexive. Spend 1 Essence. Gain Honor in Armor for the scene.<br /> <br /> -Drain (Purity): Instant. Spend 1 Willpower, roll Wits+Occult+Purity against Stamina+Resolve+Primal Urge-Purity. Successes equal essence or willpower drained. Draining essence deals agg damage to spirits.<br /> <br /> -Precision Telekinesis (Cunning): Instant. Spend 1 essence, roll Int+Occult. Add Cunning to Successes, representing dice available for any task requiring fine motor control within sight.<br /> <br /> -Ride Spirit (Glory): Extended. Spend 3 essence, roll Manipulation+Occult until 10 successes are reached, each roll representing five minutes of meditation. The spirit must be present, if not willing, to be ridden. If the spirit wishes to resist, it may roll resistance+rank. If it reaches 10 successes first, Ride Spirit may not be used upon it for a full three days. If successful, the user's soul is fettered to the spirit, her body in a trance. It does not require food. She may ride the spirit for a number of days equal to her Glory, and may make a number of 'Urged' rolls, as per page 190, adding her Glory to successes against the spirit's resistance roll, if it resists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T09:26:33-07:00","id":921522,"title":"","content":"I would swap the Renown linked to each Gift, though. Based on how each renown is described in the book, Blast could be Glory, Ride Spirit could be Cunning, Wisdom could be Precision Teleknesis. Purity and Honor as either Armor or Drain could work anyway, depending on the theme of the Gift List","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T11:24:02-07:00","id":921579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/920033-gifts-of-numen-for-your-use?p=921522#post921522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would swap the Renown linked to each Gift, though. Based on how each renown is described in the book, Blast could be Glory, Ride Spirit could be Cunning, Wisdom could be Precision Teleknesis. Purity and Honor as either Armor or Drain could work anyway, depending on the theme of the Gift List</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd put riding into Wisdom, it already has several gifts that ride beast or machinery over it's purview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T09:49:57-07:00","id":922690,"title":"","content":"Cool, thanks for the ideas. I'll probably switch em up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}